  "textHash": "554da43c7f7bfdbcfec9f6a3f9d1cad54add9f47ea544072a451c7e974ffa551",
  "text": "Notary is an agent that won't touch money until it has proven how its tools behave. It reads the docs and turns every promise into a claim. Before each test call, it commits a prediction, hashed, so it can't change afterwards. Then it calls the live API and compares. A Reflector proposes explanations. A stronger Adversary, running on a different model, tries to refute them. On our live runs, it narrowed all five beliefs instead of rubber-stamping them. What survives becomes a certificate, valid only where it was tested. No certificate, no money moves: the Guard holds anything uncovered for a person to review.",
  "durationSec": 48.823,
